/* FreeSpaceKit */
"Wipe Free Space" = "清除可用空間";
"Volume" = "磁碟區";
"Target" = "目標";
"Free now" = "目前可用空間";
"Rescan Volumes" = "重新掃描磁碟區";
"Safety reserve" = "安全保留量";
"Leave free" = "保留的可用空間";
"Free space kept unwritten so the volume never fills completely (which can crash apps or the OS). A small amount of free space is therefore left un-wiped by design." = "為避免磁碟區被完全填滿（這可能導致應用程式或作業系統當機），會保留一部分可用空間不進行寫入。因此會刻意留下少量未清除的可用空間。";
"In progress" = "進行中";
"How this works & its limits" = "運作方式及其限制";
"Only free space is overwritten. The wipe creates new files in a hidden scratch folder and fills them — the system only ever allocates unused blocks to new files, so your existing data is never read or written." = "僅會覆寫可用空間。清除作業會在隱藏的暫存檔案夾中建立新檔案並將其填滿——系統只會將未使用的區塊配置給新檔案，因此您現有的資料絕不會被讀取或寫入。";
"Corrupted, orphaned or \"ghost\" data sitting in unallocated blocks is treated as free and overwritten." = "位於未配置區塊中的損壞、孤立或「幽靈」資料會被視為可用空間並遭覆寫。";
"On SSDs (TRIM) and APFS, the platform may already have electronically erased free blocks, and wear-levelling means a logical overwrite isn't guaranteed to hit the same physical cells. This is most effective on HDDs and external/USB drives." = "在 SSD（TRIM）與 APFS 上，平台可能已經以電子方式清除了可用區塊，且由於耗損平衡，邏輯層面的覆寫並不保證會作用於相同的實體單元。此功能在 HDD 以及外接／USB 磁碟機上最為有效。";
"APFS snapshots and local Time Machine backups keep old blocks \"in use,\" so data they reference isn't free space and won't be wiped until those snapshots are removed." = "APFS 快照與本機 Time Machine 備份會將舊區塊維持為「使用中」狀態，因此它們所參照的資料並非可用空間，在這些快照被移除之前不會被清除。";
"This fills the free space on \"%@\" with %@, then removes the fill files. Your existing files are never touched — only unused space is overwritten. It can take a long time and will make the disk appear full while it runs." = "此操作會以 %@ 填滿「%@」上的可用空間，然後移除填充檔案。您現有的檔案絕不會被觸及——僅會覆寫未使用的空間。此過程可能耗時較長，且執行期間磁碟會顯示為已滿。";

